## B18 Fix - Test Isolation (2026-09-09)

### Implementation:
- Modified `tests/conftest.py`:
  - `small_config` fixture now uses `tmp_path_factory.mktemp("raw_snapshots")` for snapshot directory
  - Added `_assert_no_project_data_pollution` autouse fixture that verifies no files are written to project data directories during tests
  - Added `PROJECT_DATA_DIRS` constant to track directories that should not be polluted

### Behavior:
- All tests using `small_config` now write snapshots to temporary directories
- Tests that intentionally write to data directories can use `@pytest.mark.allow_data_dir_writes` decorator
- Snapshot tests (test_snapshots.py) already used `tmp_path` and continue to work
- After test runs, pytest will fail if any new files appeared in `data/` or `data/raw_snapshots/`

### Verification:
- Ran tests and confirmed no new files created in project data directories
- Existing snapshot files in data/ are from before the fix (pre-2026-09-09)

### Files Modified:
- tests/conftest.py (B18 fix)

